# Hashtagweb3.com Coding Rules

## Project Context
- Next.js 14 App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Supabase
- Agent-friendly platform for Web3 professionals

## API Design
- All `/api/*` routes MUST return `{ error: { code, message, hint, docUrl } }` for errors
- All `/api/*` routes MUST include CORS headers: `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`
- All `/api/*` routes MUST handle `OPTIONS` preflight requests

## TypeScript
- Avoid `any` types; use `unknown` and narrow with type guards
- Use `NextRequest` and `NextResponse` types in route handlers
- Prefer `interface` over `type` for object shapes

## Components
- Default to Server Components; add `'use client'` only when using hooks/events
- Keep components small and single-purpose
- Use semantic HTML: `<main>`, `<section>`, `<article>`, `<nav>`, `<header>`, `<footer>`

## Styling
- Tailwind CSS utility classes only; no CSS-in-JS or inline styles
- Mobile-first responsive design; use `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:` breakpoint prefixes
- Use `max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8` for consistent page width

## Agent-Readiness Requirements
- New pages MUST include relevant JSON-LD structured data
- Public content pages MUST have meaningful SSR (server-rendered) text content
- Discovery files in `public/.well-known/` MUST have corresponding route handlers
- Markdown content files MUST be served with `Content-Type: text/markdown`

## Content
- Never use placeholder text (Lorem ipsum, etc.)
- All copy must be meaningful and relevant to Web3
- Pages must include real headings, descriptions, and data
